-- title:
--   Reductions of the Igusa chart algebra span the characteristic-ℓ chart ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a positive integer $p$, a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid p$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A` has characteristic $\ell$; let $\mathrm{fm}$ be a `CharPModel.FibreModel` for level $p$ over $A$ with respect to $\ell$, $\kappa$ and the residue map $A \to \kappa$, so that in particular it provides subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$, $B_{\mathrm{inf}}$ of the base change `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull p)` (the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise images under `coeffEmb` of the level-$p$ modular function field) together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}} : B_{\mathrm{fin}} \to F_{\kappa,p}$ and $\pi_{\mathrm{inf}}$, where $F_{\kappa,p} =$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ p` is the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ p`. Assume that for every $b$ in the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra `chartAlgFin p ℓ` $=$ `chartAlg p ℓ {jFull p}` of the level-$p$ modular function field, the coefficientwise image of $b$ lies in $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$. The conclusion: every $z \in F_{\kappa,p}$ lying in `CurveModel.chartRing κ {jqModC κ}`, that is, integral over the $\kappa$-subalgebra generated by the reduced $j$-series, can be written as a finite sum $z = \sum_{i<n} c_i\, \pi_{\mathrm{fin}}(b_i)$ with $c_i \in \kappa$ (acting through the structure map of $F_{\kappa,p}$) and $b_i$ the images of elements of `chartAlgFin p ℓ`.
--
--   This is the ring-level spanning statement underlying the identification of the special fibre of the Igusa model: the characteristic-$\ell$ chart ring around $j$ is generated over the residue field by the reductions of the integral chart algebra, the characteristic-$\ell$ counterpart of `chartRing_le_span_coeffEmb_chartAlg`. It is used in the comparison of places on the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field, in [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.placeFullC_eq_congr_spPlace_of_finChart_centrePin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.placeFullC_eq_congr_spPlace_of_finChart_centrePin).
